## Installation Resources

* **VirtualBox:** Free and open-source. Download for your operating system at [VirtualBox Downloads](https://www.virtualbox.org/wiki/Downloads).
* **Ubuntu ISO:** Download the latest Desktop LTS image at [Ubuntu Desktop Download](https://ubuntu.com/download/desktop).

## Hardware Requirements

Depending on your host machine's specifications, some configurations may be resource-constrained. We recommend the following minimal host setup for a smooth experience:

* **CPU:** Multi-core processor with virtualization extensions (VT-x or AMD-V) enabled in BIOS/UEFI.
* **RAM:** At least 8 GB of system memory.
* **Storage:** At least 50 GB of free hard drive space.

## Recommended VM Configurations

Adjust the resources allocated to your VM based on your project needs:

| Profile | CPU Cores | RAM | Disk Space | Use Case |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Minimal** | 1 | 2 GB | 10 GB | Basic Linux CLI tasks |
| **Development** | 2 | 4 GB | 25 GB | IDEs, Compiling, LaTeX |
| **Heavy** | 4 | 8 GB | 50 GB | Docker, Heavy Data Processing |

> 🎬 **Video Tutorial:** A step-by-step video guide is available at [Using Ubuntu in VirtualBox](https://www.youtube.com).

